## User Review Required

> [!IMPORTANT]
> **Decision required on HITL Semantics**: The peer reviewer asks: should `reviewDurationSec > 0` for ALL 5 SYS-PROP documents, or only 2? Both are valid design choices, but they produce different Table 7 values. **The chosen definition must match the JSON.**
>
> **Proposed Resolution**: Define `reviewRequired = reviewDurationSec > 0`. Under this definition, ALL 5 SYS-PROP documents are reviewed (35s total, mean 7.0s per doc). Table 7's claim of "2 of 5" is then corrected to "5 of 5 (100%)". The `fieldsCorrected` count in Table 7 is corrected to 2 (matching the JSON sum).

> [!WARNING]
> **Latency Values**: The 23ms discrepancy in SYS-PROP mean latency (2,773 ms computed vs 2,796 ms reported) is resolved by recomputing from the JSON. No manual correction needed — the table generator will compute the correct value automatically.

> [!CAUTION]
> **`experiment_VAL-20260729.json` will be regenerated** by a new Python/TypeScript script that reads `fieldMatches`, computes correct `fieldScores`, and rewrites the file. The old file will be backed up as `experiment_VAL-20260729.ORIG.json`. **No values are manually patched** — all values flow from the canonical computation.

